      "role": "user",
      "content": "The examples are really hitting the mark. The way the manager in the first one associates the dialect with a lack of seniority or \"learning the ropes\" is exactly the kind of subtle bias we want to expose.\n\nTo finish the module, I want to round this out with a third scenario involving a technical or high-intellect role—maybe an engineer or a data scientist. Could you write a similar internal monologue for a manager interviewing a candidate who has a very heavy non-native accent (old-school immigrant style) but is clearly a genius in their field? \n\nI want the monologue to show how the manager might struggle to reconcile the candidate's obvious technical brilliance with the \"low-status\" or \"unintelligent\" vibe they get from the way the person speaks. Like, even if the candidate explains a complex algorithm perfectly, the manager still walks away feeling like \"there's something missing\" or doubting their actual competency because of the linguistic barrier.",
